# NoiseModelling Benchmark website generator

This code will download:

1. the released versions of NoiseModelling listed in `versions.json`, plus a "head" version
   (an entry with an empty URL) taken from the NoiseModelling CI artifact
2. reference input data (Clisson)

Then will run with the same parameters and output the result as a static website and publish it on github pages.

To generate the static site (linux/macos only):

```bash
bash benchmark_run.sh
```

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `versions.json` | source of truth: `version -> release zip URL` (empty URL = head version, Java 25, binary from the CI artifact) |
| `benchmark.yml` | CI: per-version Java matrix (11 for v4/v5, 25 for v6), head job, website build, Pages deploy |
| `benchmark_run.sh` | download, simulate, aggregate |
| `compare_versions.py` | pairwise comparisons (payload capped, silenced receivers excluded as NaN) |
| `generate_site.py` | builds `website/index.html` from `website/template.html` |
| `nm_version/src/main/groovy/` | simulation scripts, one per NoiseModelling version when the API changed |
| `input/clisson/` | reference dataset, stored with Git LFS |

A version is benchmarked with Java 25 when its name starts with `v6`, otherwise with Java 11.

